[quote="mwc146"]

Plus, it improves the KNYFE&#39;s synergy between cards and gives an added incentive to using Flawless Execution.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

I guess that&#39;s where I&#39;m leaning. &nbsp;I mean, the whole basis of &quot;Flawless Execution&quot; is, presumably, that KNYFE is so good that she can take out people by causing less damage than would otherwise be required. &nbsp;So if the Gauntlet only works to destroy ongoings with its own damage, that means that the Gauntlet can destroy Ongoings when KNYFE uses it sloppily, but not when she &quot;executes flawlessly&quot;? &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Can anyone think of any parallels with Fixer&#39;s Tire Iron? &nbsp; Any cases where Fixer wouldn&#39;t have done enough damage to destroy something *without* Tire Iron, only destroyed them because of Tire Iron&#39;s power, and as a result a certain event/condition doesn&#39;t trigger?

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

I&#39;ve done this with Wager Master a few times when he has &quot;Who Are You Really Fighting?&quot; out to destroy him with Tire Iron without bringing to zero and so I won because he was destroyed not brought to zero HP. &nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Slightly different case there, I think, because &quot;Who..?&quot; doesn&#39;t have a condition that triggers on destruction. &nbsp; In fact, it would be interesting to see if cards like Tire Iron, Final Dive, and Wrathful Gaze weren&#39;t exactly what Christopher had in mind when writing &quot;Who Are You Fighting?&quot; &nbsp;-- it seems tailor-made for those cards that destroy targets without reducing their HP.

&nbsp;

Killswitch has a real point, though -- does Flawless Execution act as a &#39;cardus interruptus&#39;, and so the Gauntlet&#39;s power isn&#39;t &quot;finished&quot; yet when the target is destroyed? &nbsp; &nbsp;I mean, Flawless Execution reads: &nbsp;&quot;*<strong>Whenever* damage dealt by KNYFE reduces a card to 1 HP, destroy that target.</strong>&quot; &nbsp;Unlike cards that add damage, it in effect changes the conditions for destruction of a target. &nbsp;Normally, it takes X points of damage (where X is the target&#39;s current HP) to destroy a target. &nbsp;Flawless Execution essentially changes those conditions, stating that a target is destroyed when it takes X-1 points of damage from KNYFE. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

This also addresses, to a certain extent, Matchstickman&#39;s argument above that the Gauntlet has to be read as not including Flawless Execution because otherwise it would mean that the Gauntlet&#39;s effect occurs anytime a target is destroyed sometime after KNYFE damages it with the Gauntlet. &nbsp;Flawless Execution only takes effect when KNYFE does the damage that takes the target out. &nbsp;It wouldn&#39;t activate if (ex:) KNYFE destroyed the Explosives Wagon with the Gauntlet, which then did damage that killed other targets. &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
